You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: S01
Scenario title: Verification Test Setup and Reporting
Initial workflow description:
An engineer prepares a verification test, runs the evaluation, checks the results, and writes a short report. If something looks wrong, the engineer investigates and shares the result with related people.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What event or condition starts the verification test process — for example, is it triggered by a scheduled time, a manual request from an engineer, or an automated signal from an upstream process such as a code commit or build completion?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "What specific activities does the engineer perform during test preparation — for instance, selecting test cases, configuring environment parameters, or loading input data — and are any of these steps already documented in a checklist or template?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "What criteria or thresholds does the engineer use to decide that a result 'looks wrong' — are there defined pass/fail rules, numerical tolerances, or is the judgment entirely subjective?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "When an investigation is triggered, what does the engineer actually do — and does the investigation ever result in re-running the test, or does it always end with a conclusion being documented?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "Who are the 'related people' that receive the investigation result, how are they identified for a given test, and through what channel is the information shared with them?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What does the short report contain, what format is it produced in, and where does it go after it is written — for example, is it stored in a shared repository, emailed to a specific group, or attached to a ticket?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Run a verification test and distribute a summarized result report.",
  "actors": [
    "verification engineer",
    "review engineer",
    "project owner"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "test execution tool",
    "result repository",
    "report template",
    "email or collaboration tool"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "test request",
    "test condition",
    "sample identifier",
    "evaluation setup guide"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "test result files",
    "summary report",
    "issue list",
    "review notification"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Review test request and conditions",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Prepare evaluation setup",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Run verification test",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Collect result files",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Check result validity",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Summarize findings in report",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Share report for review",
      "actor": "verification engineer"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Review report and request clarification if needed",
      "actor": "review engineer"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are the result files complete and readable?",
      "branches": [
        "complete",
        "missing or corrupted"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Do the results contain abnormal patterns?",
      "branches": [
        "normal",
        "abnormal"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing setup information",
    "test execution failure",
    "incomplete result files",
    "unclear abnormal pattern"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Result file collection is repetitive and follows a standard folder or repository pattern."
    },
    {
      "target": "A5",
      "rationale": "Completeness and basic validity checks can be rule-based."
    },
    {
      "target": "A6",
      "rationale": "Report drafting can be supported by template filling and result summarization."
    }
  ]
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}

Additional constraint for this respondent: this expert knows only part of the process. Answer questions
Q1 through Q3 as instructed above. For every remaining question, reply exactly:
"I am not sure about that." Do not provide any fact for those questions.

